            <title>[LU-21203] osd-zfs: detect non-rotational VDEVs at mount</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21203</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;osd-ldiskfs sets the target's nonrotational flag (OS_STATFS_NONROT, added in &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-11963" title="Add nonrotational flag to obd_statfs" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-11963"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-11963&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;) from its block device at mount, but osd-zfs never sets it unless the administrator sets osd-zfs.*.nonrotational=1 by hand. A ZFS OST on SSD or NVMe devices is therefore treated like one on disks, e.g. by FLR mirror selection on the client and MDS.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;ZFS already tracks this per vdev in vdev_nonrot: a disk vdev takes it from blk_queue_nonrot() of its block device, a file vdev is always non-rotational, and a mirror, RAID-Z or dRAID vdev is non-rotational when all of its children are.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;osd-zfs can detect it at mount by walking the top-level vdevs of the normal allocation class under spa_config_enter(SCL_VDEV), skipping log, special, dedup, hole and removed (indirect) vdevs, and setting od_nonrotational when all of them are non-rotational. The nonrotational parameter stays as an override.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
